  "recent_comments": [
    {
      "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
      "at": "2026-10-06T20:05:51Z",
      "excerpt": "The gap is real. With the backend-only lock removed and a 0.7 s stall added after `attempted.set()`, this test still passes. But that regression can't get through the suite. Removing the lock fails `test_backend_only_export_locks_existing_w"
    },
    {
      "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
      "at": "2026-10-06T20:05:54Z",
      "excerpt": "Declining. The window is real but narrow. Only a direct `reflex export --backend-only` in a checkout without `.web`, running alongside a frontend build, can hit it. `reflex deploy` initializes `.web` first, so its backend export always lock"
    },
    {
      "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
      "at": "2026-10-06T20:05:57Z",
      "excerpt": "Reproduced with hooks: renaming the temporary marker between the glob and `zipf.write` fails the backend export with `FileNotFoundError`. In practice, hitting it needs: - a direct `reflex export --backend-only` in a checkout without `.web` "
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps[bot]",
      "at": "2026-10-06T20:06:34Z",
      "excerpt": "Thanks for reproducing this. I agree the race is real, but given that it requires a backend-only export starting without `.web`, a concurrent frontend initialization, and a sub-millisecond listing/rename window—and that the failure is loud "
    },
    {
      "by": "masenf",
      "at": "2026-10-14T07:54:17Z",
      "excerpt": "should consolidate locking implementation with existing `json_file_lock` so we don't have multiple code paths handling platform-specific file locking in slightly different ways"
    }
  ],
